{
  "name": "ship-dev",
  "description": "Ship's own dev loop as a Ship pipeline. Implement → verify → review, one shared worktree, auto-merge on success.",
  "auto_merge": true,
  "steps": [
    { "id": "implement", "agent": "rust-lane", "provider": "{{ provider }}" },
    {
      "id": "verify",
      "run": "cargo check --workspace 2>&1 | tail -5\ncargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast 2>&1 | tail -10\n",
      "after": ["implement"]
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "agent": "gatekeeper",
      "after": ["verify"],
      "gate": {
        "require_changed": [{ "match": ["**/*.rs"], "min": 1 }],
        "forbid_changed": [{ "match": [".artifacts/**"], "min": 0 }]
      }
    }
  ],
  "step_specs": [
    "# Implementer — step 1 of 3\n\nExecute the spec at `.artifacts/pipeline/spec.md`. Make the requested change, write tests if behavior is changing, ensure `cargo check` passes locally before signalling done.\n\n**Completion rule:** the moment `cargo check` and the relevant `cargo test` pass once, run `ship ops call pipelines.step_done --json '{\"slug\":\"'\"'$SHIP_ACTOR_ID'\"'\",\"summary\":\"one-line summary (files changed, test count)\"}'` to signal completion and stop. Do not run additional verification rounds — the verify step (next) will do that for you.\n",
    "# Verify — step 2 of 3 (shell only, no agent)\n\n`cargo check` and `cargo test` run in the same worktree the implementer used. Reuses the implementer's compiled artifacts (target/ is shared). Exit non-zero on any test failure — pipeline halts before review.\n",
    "# Reviewer — step 3 of 3\n\nGrade the implementer's work against `.artifacts/pipeline/spec.md`:\n1. Did the change accomplish the spec's stated goal?\n2. Are tests present where behavior changed?\n3. Diff stays inside the spec's allowed file scope?\n\nVerdict: `ship ops call pipelines.step_done --json '{\"slug\":\"'\"'$SHIP_ACTOR_ID'\"'\",\"summary\":\"pass/fail + evidence\"}'` to signal completion. On fail, quote the offending diff hunk.\n"
  ]
}
